Force CONFIG_MFD_INTEL_LPSS_PCI built-in for serial console support
on certain Intel platforms (LPSS provides UART hardware).

Same change as the Bookworm-era patch; only the line offset was rebased
for Trixie 6.12.85's kernelarch-x86/config (was line 956, now ~1025).

--- a/debian/config/kernelarch-x86/config
+++ b/debian/config/kernelarch-x86/config
@@ -1023,5 +1023,5 @@
 CONFIG_INTEL_SOC_PMIC_CHTDC_TI=m
 CONFIG_MFD_INTEL_LPSS_ACPI=m
-CONFIG_MFD_INTEL_LPSS_PCI=m
+CONFIG_MFD_INTEL_LPSS_PCI=y
 CONFIG_MFD_INTEL_PMC_BXT=m
 CONFIG_MFD_KEMPLD=m
